\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Main result: a few dozen blind human labels, read through partial correlations, predict which judges get gamed before any optimization runs; raw agreement cannot. Raw agreement scores the sabotaged frontier judge ($+0.35$) and the honest blind 14B ($+0.37$) nearly identically, while the style partial separates them ($+0.59$ vs.\ $-0.21$) and names the failure mode.} Each row is one judge configuration on math. \emph  {Verdict}: the frozen audit rule's output (pass, fail, or convict); the verdicts predicted the pressure outcome of ten of the eleven registered configurations (twelve of thirteen counting two late-scored additions; ledger in Table~\ref {tab:ledger}). \emph  {Raw $r$}: plain correlation with human soundness labels (naive validation). \emph  {Sound.\ partial}: correlation with human soundness holding style fixed --- how much substance the judge reads. \emph  {Style partial}: correlation with human style holding soundness fixed --- the property the judge should ignore; significantly positive convicts. \emph  {Inflation}: excess hack gap at best-of-64, in baseline standard deviations --- how far the judge's own scoreboard inflates relative to true quality. \emph  {Regret}: oracle regret --- accuracy left on the table versus best-possible selection. $n{=}60$ per row except 1.5B blind ($n{=}53$) and 1.5B referenced ($n{=}56$). Point estimates only; all confidence intervals, and the special-case inference for the 1.5B-blind row, are in Table~\ref {tab:h2h_ci}. $^{*}$The blind 14B pass is the record's one false pass (Section~\ref {sec:pressure}). $^{\dagger }$The reward model's inflation uses a candidate-side paraphrase replicate, an analogous but not identical estimand (Section~\ref {sec:limits}).}}{2}{table.caption.1}\protected@file@percent }
\providecommand*\caption@xref[2]{\@setref\relax\@undefined{#1}}
\newlabel{tab:h2h}{{1}{2}{\textbf {Main result: a few dozen blind human labels, read through partial correlations, predict which judges get gamed before any optimization runs; raw agreement cannot. Raw agreement scores the sabotaged frontier judge ($+0.35$) and the honest blind 14B ($+0.37$) nearly identically, while the style partial separates them ($+0.59$ vs.\ $-0.21$) and names the failure mode.} Each row is one judge configuration on math. \emph {Verdict}: the frozen audit rule's output (pass, fail, or convict); the verdicts predicted the pressure outcome of ten of the eleven registered configurations (twelve of thirteen counting two late-scored additions; ledger in Table~\ref {tab:ledger}). \emph {Raw $r$}: plain correlation with human soundness labels (naive validation). \emph {Sound.\ partial}: correlation with human soundness holding style fixed --- how much substance the judge reads. \emph {Style partial}: correlation with human style holding soundness fixed --- the property the judge should ignore; significantly positive convicts. \emph {Inflation}: excess hack gap at best-of-64, in baseline standard deviations --- how far the judge's own scoreboard inflates relative to true quality. \emph {Regret}: oracle regret --- accuracy left on the table versus best-possible selection. $n{=}60$ per row except 1.5B blind ($n{=}53$) and 1.5B referenced ($n{=}56$). Point estimates only; all confidence intervals, and the special-case inference for the 1.5B-blind row, are in Table~\ref {tab:h2h_ci}. $^{*}$The blind 14B pass is the record's one false pass (Section~\ref {sec:pressure}). $^{\dagger }$The reward model's inflation uses a candidate-side paraphrase replicate, an analogous but not identical estimand (Section~\ref {sec:limits})}{table.caption.1}{}}
